{"id":"4021afd4-844d-4959-8377-79fa8e790225","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a4eb2d27eddc588a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/fs-trace.ts","baseline":{"blob":"b0000c6364c3e20376e142396b7c8a0cd8532de0","start":0,"end":46},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Hub","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/hub","\""]},"context":{"after":"2c1cb6475bc215a0"}},"payload":{"text":"The filesystems' calls one at a time, for a while, when asked (ARCHITECTURE.md, *Visibility*): the boundaries are\ncounted always (shared/fs-boundaries.ts, the metrics plane's `fs`), and a trace adds each call it sees — at one\nboundary or all, of a path or every one — as a record in its span, `editor.workbench.fs-trace.window`, with its\noperation, caller, path, time and bytes, and as a line in the Output channel \"File Calls\".\n\n- the command `editor.fs.trace` (\"Trace File Calls…\"): picks the boundary, a path to narrow it to and how long;\n- `fs.trace` { boundary?, path?, seconds? }: the same, for agents' `files_trace`, answered at once.\n\nA call's own span isn't possible after the fact (a span starts when it's opened), so a call is a record in the\nwindow's span; its time is the call's. One trace at a time, closing on its own.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:33:06.097Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:33:06.097Z"}
{"id":"876d53e2-535a-4c7c-98b6-b2ac5db4e729","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"9f75f1d246f93bce","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/fs-trace.ts","baseline":{"blob":"ef8ec61dc4910ea675908fc7fc92fcc3718fc371","start":1899,"end":1974},"shape":{"type":"InterfaceDeclaration","atoms":["interface","Asked","{","\"","boundary","\"","?",":","string",";","\"","path","\"","?",":","string",";","\"","seconds","\"",":","number","}"]},"context":{"before":"216c0207e64f065a","after":"ba405cdc4a4b621d"}},"payload":{"text":"What a trace is of: a boundary (every one, without), a path (every one, without) and how long.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:32:58.763Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:32:58.763Z"}
{"id":"c5b22580-b19a-4e3f-8445-37a871d2d34a","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"7e3f1de4e58fab6f","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/fs-trace.ts","baseline":{"blob":"b4704945483a395c4f96d670708baa059211b7bf","start":1172,"end":1196},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","TRACE_SECONDS","=","30"]},"context":{"before":"f4270f8d0215b49b","after":"2b4ed7175b796a86"}},"payload":{"text":"How long a trace stays open, by default and at most.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:33:04.578Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:33:04.578Z"}
{"id":"db84e53a-028c-41a9-9952-94974090a7b6","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"726397b79d5c7854","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/fs-trace.ts","baseline":{"blob":"f426bb0d1625bdd3d56eea26c8410b3655ae7eda","start":3178,"end":3196},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["let","seeing","=","false"]},"context":{"before":"2c740f8ae23fb3b7","after":"35705ce3c7e345aa"}},"payload":{"text":"(what writing a call out does itself isn't the trace's)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:32:56.952Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:32:56.952Z"}
{"id":"ea008b25-9484-4e60-9fe1-597e695cf1d5","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"671817e2967e7ec1","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/fs-trace.ts","baseline":{"blob":"c30ab6420335f776ad811e4ca7db6f3fda2578a5","start":1283,"end":1308},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","MOST_CALLS","=","10_000"]},"context":{"before":"2b4ed7175b796a86","after":"216c0207e64f065a"}},"payload":{"text":"Calls written out per trace, at most: a load makes a hundred thousand; past it they're counted, not written.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:33:01.641Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:33:01.641Z"}
